  :contracts [
    (:contract :id D81PlanContext :text "This is an amended prospective plan under the user-authorized breaking-change policy; no implementation completion or semantic baseline is claimed. On loading a task, resolve every contractRef and contractRefs entry from this ledger before acting; missing or unknown contract identity is a hard planning error.")
    (:contract :id D81SettledChoices :text "The canonical ADR and this ledger settle compatibility breaks, native/WASM backends, optional local serve, experimental package retention and canonical projections. Later changes require evidence-backed task amendment rather than silently changing a gate.")
    (:contract :id D81TaskFailureModes :text "Unavailable oracle, target or authorized model access leaves readiness/acceptance pending. Concurrent overlap requires the dependency chain and per-file lease. Source or gate changes invalidate old receipts. Preserve prior audit receipts as history, never current evidence.")
    (:contract :id D81BehavioralAcceptance :text "The task command invokes verifier-owned tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh with one exact task ID; that trusted outer supervisor runs the corresponding ASL oracle, captures actual process status and observed diagnostics/effects, validates passing and forced-failing oracle sentinels, then requires every task verificationCase and required assertion outcome. No label-only, file-existence-only or generic nonzero result establishes semantic success/failure. Supervisor shell infrastructure is temporary independent verification, not a shipped runtime dependency. Plan syntax acceptance is separate.")
    (:contract :id D81Baseline :text "First ratify the canonical target contract without changing production implementation. The independent verifier then freezes hidden vectors and establishes the intended failure on the captured source baseline using the trusted outer supervisor, positive control and forced-failing oracle sentinel. Until ASL failure propagation is established, the host supervisor independently checks expected process status, diagnostics and effects; an unexecuted or unknown-symbol oracle cannot pass. Missing fixture/command, parse error or unavailable environment is readiness failure, never semantic red evidence. Every task baseline is currently notEstablished; new features require a specific absent-capability observation, not an arbitrary missing-script failure.")
    (:contract :id D81Ownership :text "Implementation writers own source and public development tests; verificationOwns paths and runner configuration are authored/controlled by an independent verifier. Final implementation review is a distinct identity from its writer and oracle author where feasible. Overlapping writers follow the dependency chain and per-file lease. Rendered rule edits originate in owned canonical source. Future acceptance paths need not exist during planning.")
    (:contract :id D81Receipts :text "A trusted local verifier records session, step, exact gate, source/artifact digests, real exit status, executed cases and relevant mutation/semantic outcomes. The model cannot authorize itself with a receipt string/hash. Changed source or gate invalidates old receipts; replay and wrong-step binding fail. Until runner binding exists, an independent verifier records physical execution receipts outside author write access; no readiness waiver counts as implementation completion.")
    (:contract :id D81PlanGate :text "Plan syntax, unique IDs, acyclic dependencies, review-disposition coverage and declared ownership are structural checks only. Approving this plan settles design and sequencing, not runtime correctness or already established behavioral baselines.")
    (:verificationBoundary :owns ["tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh" "tests/acceptance/d81"] :owner "independentVerifier" :policy "No implementation author can read or modify hidden acceptance, supervisor configuration or its issuer identity; public development tests remain separate.")
  ]
  :ruleDispositions [
    (:rule :id tools :disposition :confirm :tasks ["Task43603" "Task43705"] :resolution "Prefer available structural RPC, inspect item payload/errors, permit truthful host fallback; no speed claim.")
    (:rule :id context :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43702" "Task43902" "Task44102"] :resolution "Stable base plus relevant dynamic context; provider-scoped cache evidence, no universal price or AST retrieval superiority.")
    (:rule :id output :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43806" "Task44104" "Task44106"] :resolution "Preserve typed evidence and recoverable references; distinguish reversible encoding/deduplication from lossy omission; evaluate compression empirically.")
    (:rule :id names :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43806" "Task43807"] :resolution "Meaningful conventional names and scoped case consistency; no universal token percentages or alias ban where domain meaning warrants aliases.")
    (:rule :id semantics :disposition :confirm :tasks ["Task43601" "Task43602" "Task43801" "Task44001"] :resolution "Imports bind, unknown symbols fail, test results are explicit; observable canonical semantics replace assertion-count parity.")
    (:rule :id gates :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43605" "Task43901"] :resolution "Require intended semantic negative controls and actual producer status; separate reachability, assertion inversion, production faults and correctness.")
    (:rule :id grading :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43901" "Task43903" "Task44105"] :resolution "Different implementation author and final verifier with protected oracles; fresh role prose alone is not independence.")
    (:rule :id concepts :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43706" "Task43806"] :resolution "Label principles, hypotheses and measurements; empirical numbers require scoped primary evidence, policies may remain explicit principles.")
    (:rule :id foreign :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43607" "Task43803" "Task44002" "Task44003"] :resolution "Owned semantics and autonomous deployed tool, explicit seed/build/test/OS boundaries; no necessary third-party compiler/runtime in deployment.")
    (:rule :id git :disposition :confirm :tasks ["Task43706"] :resolution "User-authorized intended-only changes and base/log checks remain principles; no new performance justification or publication permission.")
    (:rule :id parallel :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43808" "Task44110"] :resolution "Parallel independent reads and owned partitions, conflict serialization and per-session progression; four/six agent limits are configurable policy, not measured optima.")
    (:rule :id anchor :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task44101" "Task44106"] :resolution "External durable state with capability-aware fallback; no fixed compliance-decay or proven-restoration claim.")
    (:rule :id oneStep :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43808" "Task44101"] :resolution "One authorized transaction/step per session with batch edits inside its owned write set and source-bound verifier completion.")
    (:rule :id budget :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43902" "Task44104" "Task44106"] :resolution "Tunable explicit budgets, relevant static checks for read-only work, no universal six-call threshold or exclusive-compaction claim.")
    (:rule :id hiddenTests :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task43601" "Task44105"] :resolution "Public development tests are readable/authorable within owns; hidden independent acceptance and runner configuration are isolated across all tools.")
    (:rule :id bounded :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task44103"] :resolution "Relevant complete small files are allowed; aggregate and per-child limits, recoverable versioned continuation, no universal context-length law.")
    (:rule :id edge :disposition :amend :tasks ["Task44108"] :resolution "Declared reversible containment/refutation/escalation procedure; immediate escalation for absent authority or unsafe containment; no mandatory mutation.")
    (:rule :id ssot :disposition :confirm :tasks ["Task43707" "Task43806" "Task44109"] :resolution "Canonical rules render into deterministic per-client/tier projections; register-or-fail surfaces, ownership includes canonical source, no hand edits.")
  ]
